@node 20260904_dev "20260904-dev"
@{b}20260904-dev@{ub}

@{i}Components in this release@{ui}:

  * @{fg shine}ptable.library 2.0-dev (27.08.2026)@{fg text} @{i}(new)@{ui}
  * @{fg shine}lsptres 1.0-dev (27.08.2026)@{fg text} @{i}(new)@{ui}

@{b}New major version of ptable.library 2.0@{ub}

  * @{b}Unified partition scanning.@{ub} One scanner parses RDB, MBR, GPT and flat
    (whole-disk FAT) tables and publishes every partition into @{fg shine}partition.resource@{fg text}
    , the shared partition manager. Any driver or handler reads the layout from
    there instead of parsing the card itself; @{fg shine}compactflash.device@{fg text} and @{fg shine}fat95@{fg text} do
    today. See @{"  ptable.guide  " link "ptable.guide/Main"} .
  * @{b}Selectable filesystem for MBR/GPT FAT partitions.@{ub} The consumer can name the
    DosType to mount them with ( @{fg shine}mc_NodeDosType@{fg text} ) and a handler to load when
    @{fg shine}FileSystem.resource@{fg text} has none ( @{fg shine}mc_NodeHandler@{fg text} ). Unset means unchanged; RDB
    partitions are unaffected.
  * @{b}@{fg shine}lsptres@{fg text}@{ub} shows the DosType a mounted partition actually carries in its @{fg shine}DosType@{fg text}
    column. A handler that mounts statically can record its DosType too, via a new
    @{fg shine}RegisterPartition@{fg text} input.

@{b}New tool 'lsptres 1.0'@{ub}

  * Lists the contents of @{fg shine}partition.resource@{fg text}. See @{"  lsptres.guide  " link "lsptres.guide/Main"}.

----------------------------------------
